               happiness, sadness, or anger. We have implemented an interface
               between that system and the embodied conversational agent Greta,
               developed at the University of Rome ``La Sapienza'' and
               ``University of Paris 8''. We model expressivity of the facial
               animation of the agent with a set of six dimensions that
               characterize the manner of behavior execution. In this paper we
               will first describe a mapping between the acoustic cues and the
               expressivity dimensions of the face. Then we will show how to
               determine the facial expression corresponding to the emotional
               intention resulting from the acoustic analysis, using music
